  "question": {
    "text": "When aluminium is bombarded with fast neutrons, it changes into sodium with emission of particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> according to the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Al</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>13</mn><mn>27</mn></mmultiscripts><msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><msubsup><mo>→</mo><mn>11</mn><mn>24</mn></msubsup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br />\rWhat is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Electron",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Proton",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Neutron",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Alpha- particle",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The mass number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and its atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br />Hence particle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is the helium nucleus, which is called an alpha particle"
  }
